# Benchmark run artifacts — timestamped output of benchmark/prinasa-runner.ts
# (38+ files per run). Regenerate with `bun run bench:prinasa`. Kept out of the
# tree so `git status` stays reviewable; ground-truth-failures.json and cited
# benchmark reports/results are tracked deliberately so reports are reproducible on clone.
benchmark/results/*.json
!benchmark/results/ground-truth-failures.json
# Head-to-head vs a standard vector-RAG baseline, judged by a different model family.
!benchmark/results/rag-comparison-store.json
!benchmark/results/cognee-1000-results.json
!benchmark/results/cognee-1000-report.json
!benchmark/results/cognee-1000-bm25.json
!benchmark/results/supermemory-1000.json
# Cited as the source of benchmark/results/entity-hop-decision.md, so it must be
# readable from a clone — same rule as the other cited result files above.
!benchmark/results/entity-hop-ablation.json
!benchmark/results/real-prose-arm.json
!benchmark/results/entity-hop-tune.json
!benchmark/results/fusion-k-sweep.json

# Third-party tool scaffolding (impeccable critique system). Installed locally
# per developer, not project source: nothing under src/ or the build references
# it, and .github/skills/impeccable/scripts/live-browser.js is a 500KB+ bundle
# that made every lint run print a Babel deoptimisation warning.
.github/skills/
.github/agents/
.github/hooks/
.github/impeccable.json

# Backup of the live LLM config taken by trial/live scripts. Holds an ENCRYPTED api key
# plus the baseUrl/model; it is machine-local state, not a fixture, so it must never be
# committed. It was untracked-but-not-ignored, which left it one `git add -A` from landing.
trial/live/.llmconfig.backup.json
trial/live/.llmconfig.json

# local Windows launcher
start.bat

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UAT / audit scratch output at the repo ROOT.
#
# MEASURED: 61 files (6.2 MB) of screenshots, DOM dumps and probe JSON sat untracked-ish at the root and then landed
# in ONE commit (`c3592be`, whose message is about a guardrail fix) because nothing ignored them. They were the
# evidence for a UAT round — genuinely useful at the time — but a repo root is not where evidence lives.
#
# The ruled-out alternative was a blanket `*.png` / `*.txt`: the repo legitimately tracks a few text assets, and a
# broad ignore silently swallows a real fixture the first time someone adds one. These patterns name the SHAPES the
# scratch output actually takes, so a deliberate asset at the root still needs an explicit `!`.
#
# Evidence belongs in docs/ (prose + linked artefacts) or a report file, where a reader can find it later. If you
# need to keep a screenshot, put it under docs/ and commit it on purpose.
# Scoped to the ROOT ONLY (`/`), because these folders legitimately hold the same extensions and a global pattern
# would hide the next real asset added there: docs/screenshots/ (7 tracked PNGs), test-data/wikipedia/ (15 tracked
# .txt fixtures), public/robots.txt, helm/templates/NOTES.txt. Already-tracked files keep working either way — the
# damage a global pattern does is SILENT, to the next file someone adds on purpose.
/*.png
/*.txt
# Probe/scan dumps written by ad-hoc Playwright and DOM inspection: a bare single-word filename ending in .json.
# Deliberately NOT `*.json` — package.json, tsconfig.json, components.json and the tracked coverage summary all live
# at the root, and a broad ignore would have hidden the coverage artifact the release gate reads.
/nav.json
/views.json
/dom_probe.json
/settings_tabs.json
/stage1.json
/a11y_monitoring.json

# Agent-run artefacts: 34 MB of downloaded PDFs and scratch scripts, not product code.
# The REPORTS are the point of a run, so they stay tracked; everything else does not.
uat/agent-runs/**
!uat/agent-runs/*/
!uat/agent-runs/*/REPORT.md

# Generated portable plugin SDK
/sdk/dist/
